"email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-05T21:29:21Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix(background): discard stale pre-captured screenshots — 10s max age guard\n\nWhen the content script''s 8s screenshot timeout fires, the pending\nscreenshot in the background service worker was never consumed and\nwould be returned for the next session, showing the wrong viewport.\n\nTrack pendingScreenshotTime at capture and discard anything older than\n10s when the content script requests it, falling back to live capture.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"23f921e8008af9d4762b25a8e56fddffda37e8b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/trees/23f921e8008af9d4762b25a8e56fddffda37e8b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/commits/7275d0ff6b128a606212f2148ed49589c9629924","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/7275d0ff6b128a606212f2148ed49589c9629924","node_id":"C_kwDOQkfx6toAKDcyNzVkMGZmNmIxMjhhNjA2MjEyZjIxNDhlZDQ5NTg5Yzk2Mjk5MjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e","sha":"7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e"}],"sha":"7275d0ff6b128a606212f2148ed49589c9629924","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/7275d0ff6b128a606212f2148ed49589c9629924"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-04T04:58:03Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-04T04:58:03Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Frame OS Phase 5A — frame-agent routing, screenshot capture, dev tooling (#22)\n\n* feat: Add Claude Code integration via MCP server\n\nImplements bi-directional communication between MrPlug browser extension\nand Claude Code terminal using the Model Context Protocol (MCP).\n\n## Features\n\n- **MCP Server**: Standalone Node.js server bridging Claude ↔ Browser\n- **Browser MCP Client**: WebSocket + REST client in extension\n- **7 MCP Tools**: Claude can discover, query, and control browser\n- **Bi-directional Communication**: Real-time updates and commands\n- **Session Management**: Access feedback sessions from terminal\n\n## Components Added\n\n### MCP Server (mrplug-mcp-server/)\n- src/server.ts - MCP protocol implementation with tools\n- src/browser-plugin-manager.ts - State management\n- src/http-server.ts - WebSocket & REST API server\n- src/stdio-server.ts - Claude Code STDIO transport\n- Full TypeScript support with 147 dependencies\n\n### Browser Extension Integration\n- src/lib/mcp-client.ts - WebSocket client with auto-reconnect\n- src/background/index.ts - MCP client initialization\n- src/types/index.ts - MCP configuration types\n\n### Documentation & Config\n- CLAUDE_INTEGRATION.md - Complete setup guide\n- IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md - Technical details\n- .claude/config.json - Auto-configuration for Claude Code\n- start-mcp-server.sh - Quick start script\n\n## MCP Tools for Claude\n\n1. get_browser_state - Plugin status and active sessions\n2. get_active_session - Full session details\n3. get_element_context - DOM element info (styles, position)\n4. send_browser_command - Control browser (open, select, screenshot)\n5. list_feedback_sessions - List all sessions\n6. query_session_history - Get conversation messages\n7. add_session_message - Add messages to sessions\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start MCP Server\n```bash\ncd mrplug-mcp-server\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n### Enable in Browser Extension\n- Settings → Enable MCP Integration\n- Server URL: http://localhost:3001\n- WebSocket URL: ws://localhost:3002\n\n### Use with Claude Code\n```\n\"What feedback sessions are active?\"\n\"Show me the button element details\"\n\"Open the browser to that element\"\n```\n\n## Technical Stack\n\n- Model Context Protocol SDK v1.0.4\n- WebSocket (ws) for real-time communication\n- Express for REST API\n- TypeScript with full type safety\n- Auto-reconnection with exponential backoff\n\n## Security Note\n\n⚠️ Current implementation is for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY\n- No authentication\n- CORS enabled for all origins\n- Designed for localhost use\n\nSee CLAUDE_INTEGRATION.md for production recommendations.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Add quick start guide for Claude Code integration\n\n* docs: Add comprehensive MCP integration documentation\n\nDocuments the complete MCP + Claude Code integration work including:\n- Full architecture and implementation details\n- All modified files with line references\n- API endpoints and message formats\n- WebSocket streaming implementation\n- Known stability issues and why it was paused\n- Steps to resume in future (estimated 2-3 days)\n\nAlso includes:\n- CURRENT_STATUS.md - Current state and next steps\n- READY_TO_TEST.md - Quick testing guide\n- STREAMING_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md - Guide for Claude Code\n- CLAUDE_CODE_BLOGENGINE_INSTRUCTIONS.md - MCP tool reference\n\nThe MCP integration was functional but deemed too unstable for\ninitial release due to WebSocket complexity, connection management,\nand operational overhead. Preserving all code and documentation\nfor future iteration.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add MCP server and client infrastructure (preserved)\n\nImplements bi-directional communication between browser extension\nand Claude Code via Model Context Protocol server.\n\nMCP Server (mrplug-mcp-server):\n- HTTP REST API on port 3001\n- WebSocket server on port 3002\n- Browser plugin state management\n- Implementation request queue\n- Progress broadcasting system\n\nBrowser Extension Components:\n- MCPClient - WebSocket client for real-time communication\n- MCPDebugPanel - Activity monitor UI component\n- ChatMessage - Enhanced message display with debug info\n- chat-helpers - Message creation utilities\n\nThis infrastructure is preserved but not active in the extension.\nSee docs/MCP_CLAUDE_CODE_INTEGRATION.md for full details.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add GitHub issue integration\n\nEnables creating GitHub issues directly from feedback suggestions.\n\nFeatures:\n- Click GitHub issue suggestions to create issues automatically\n- Full context included in issue body (element, page URL, screenshot)\n- Priority-based labeling (mrplug, priority-high/medium/low)\n- Prompts to configure GitHub token/repo if not set\n- Opens settings page for easy configuration\n\nIssue body includes:\n- User feedback description\n- Element details and context\n- Page URL where feedback originated\n- Screenshot (if available)\n- Created via MrPlug attribution\n\nThis provides a stable, async workflow for implementing fixes\nthrough GitHub''s infrastructure instead of real-time MCP connection.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add settings page navigation improvements\n\nEnhances settings page UX by returning to the referring tab after saving.\n\nFeatures:\n- Clicking \"Save Settings\" returns to previous browser tab\n- Settings tab closes automatically after save\n- Graceful fallback if referring tab was closed\n- Message handler in background script for open-settings\n\nBackground script (src/background/index.ts):\n- Tracks referring tab ID when opening settings\n- Stores tab ID in local storage\n- Opens existing settings tab if already open\n\nOptions page (src/options/index.tsx):\n- Reads referring tab ID on save\n- Switches back to referring tab\n- Closes settings tab after short delay\n- Cleans up stored tab ID\n\nImproves workflow by reducing tab switching friction when\nconfiguring GitHub tokens or other settings.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Replace MCP integration with GitHub workflow in FeedbackModal\n\nRemoves unstable MCP integration and finalizes GitHub-based workflow.\n\nRemoved:\n- handleClaudeCodeAction() - MCP implementation requests\n- MCP connection status checking\n- MCP activity tracking and debug panel\n- MCP progress event listeners\n- WebSocket message handling\n\nAdded:\n- handleGitHubIssue() - GitHub issue creation from suggestions\n- GitHub configuration prompts\n- Progress messages for issue creation\n- Error handling for GitHub API\n\nChanges:\n- Action handler only supports ''github-issue'' and ''manual'' types\n- Removed ''claude-code'' action type\n- Simplified config loading (no MCP status check)\n- Cleaned up imports (no MCPDebugPanel, ProgressMessages)\n\nThis completes the transition from real-time MCP communication to\nasync GitHub-based workflow, which is more stable and doesn''t\nrequire running a separate MCP server.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Delete all MCP implementation code\n\nRemoves all MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration code that was\ndeemed too unstable for initial release.\n\nDeleted:\n- mrplug-mcp-server/ - Complete MCP server directory\n- src/lib/mcp-client.ts - WebSocket client\n- src/components/MCPDebugPanel.tsx - Debug UI\n- src/components/ChatMessage.tsx - MCP-focused message component\n- src/lib/chat-helpers.ts - MCP helper utilities\n- docs/MCP_CLAUDE_CODE_INTEGRATION.md - MCP documentation\n- READY_TO_TEST.md, STREAMING_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md\n- CLAUDE_CODE_BLOGENGINE_INSTRUCTIONS.md, CURRENT_STATUS.md\n\nChanges to FeedbackModal.tsx:\n- Removed ChatMessage component usage\n- Removed createProgressMessage helper\n- Added simple inline message renderer\n- Added createStatusMessage helper for status updates\n- Simplified message display (no MCP debug info)\n\nRationale:\nMCP integration was functional but unstable due to WebSocket\ncomplexity, connection management issues, and operational overhead.\nFocusing on GitHub-based workflow as a more stable alternative.\n\nA GitHub issue will be created to document what was attempted,\nwhat didn''t work, and potential future improvements.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: gitignore core-managed symlinks (domain-knowledge/, .claude/commands/)\n\nInstalled by core/scripts/install-agents.sh — not owned by this repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Frame OS integration — visual identity, Cmd+Shift+F, AI to background\n\n- Frame tokens: copy shell tokens.css → src/styles/frame-tokens.css (--ojf-* single source)\n- carbon-lite.css now imports frame-tokens instead of hand-rolled vars\n- #mrplug-root always uses cds--g100 — Frame dark, host-page-agnostic\n- Cursor-mode indicator redesigned as fixed top bar (Frame surface, ojf-accent border, slide-in)\n- Command+Shift+F (mac) replaces MacCtrl+Shift+F; Escape added as exit key\n- FeedbackModal heading shows element selector instead of static string\n- Manifest: *.jim.software added to host_permissions + content_scripts\n- AI calls moved from content script to background worker (browser.runtime.sendMessage)\n- Content bundle: 906KB → 254KB (72% reduction — no AI SDK in content)\n- Added CLAUDE.md with invariants and phase roadmap\n- Deleted 14 pre-core-era markdown files from root\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(background): route AI through frame-agent in dev mode\n\nIn dev builds (env.json present), frameAgentUrl is auto-configured to\nhttp://localhost:4001. The ai-request handler tries POST /api/inspect\non frame-agent first; falls back to direct AIAgent if frame-agent is\nunreachable or returns an error — ensuring production users with their\nown API key are unaffected.\n\n- types/index.ts: add frameAgentUrl?: string to ExtensionConfig\n- background/index.ts: frame-agent fetch with graceful fallback;\n  auto-sets frameAgentUrl in both startup and install auto-configure paths\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wake MV3 service worker on activate to prevent screenshot timeout\n\nThe service worker sleeps after ~30s of inactivity. When the user\nclicks an element, captureVisibleTab() never fires if the SW is cold,\ncausing the 3s timeout to win every time.\n\nFix:\n- activate() sends a fire-and-forget ping to wake the SW while the\n  user is still in cursor mode (before they click anything)\n- background handles ''ping'' → { pong: true } to keep the SW awake\n- timeout raised 3s → 8s to cover SW cold-start (3–5s in practice)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: pre-capture screenshot at command time + fix double-toggle\n\nTwo root causes for missing screenshot thumbnails:\n\n1. captureVisibleTab() requires an activeTab grant, which only exists\n   when the Chrome extension command fires. The content script''s own\n   keydown handler doesn''t grant it. Fix: capture the screenshot\n   immediately in commands.onCommand while activeTab is guaranteed,\n   cache it in pendingScreenshot, and return it on the next\n   ''capture-screenshot'' request. Live capture is kept as fallback.\n\n2. Both the content script keydown handler AND Chrome''s command path\n   call toggleActive(), causing immediate deactivation. Fix: record\n   keydownActivatedAt timestamp; ignore ''toggle-feedback'' messages\n   that arrive within 300ms of a keydown-triggered activation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: expand host_permissions to <all_urls>, update popup for jim.software\n\n- Replace four specific host_permissions with <all_urls> so\n  captureVisibleTab() works from the live-capture fallback path even\n  when the extension was activated via content script keydown (no\n  activeTab grant). Specific host patterns are still enforced by the\n  content_scripts.matches list.\n\n- Popup URL validation: accept *.jim.software in addition to localhost\n  and 127.0.0.1 (matches the content_scripts.matches list)\n\n- Keyboard shortcut help text: Cmd+Shift+F replaces fn-F1, Esc added,\n  copy updated to match actual behaviour\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2be29ce6a4b6da7dcb496db00f75f41a966d3287","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/trees/2be29ce6a4b6da7dcb496db00f75f41a966d3287"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/commits/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e","verification":{"payload":"tree 2be29ce6a4b6da7dcb496db00f75f41a966d3287\nparent c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe\nauthor ojfbot <151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com> 1772600283 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1772600283 -0600\n\nfeat: Frame OS Phase 5A — frame-agent routing, screenshot capture, dev tooling (#22)\n\n* feat: Add Claude Code integration via MCP server\n\nImplements bi-directional communication between MrPlug browser extension\nand Claude Code terminal using the Model Context Protocol (MCP).\n\n## Features\n\n- **MCP Server**: Standalone Node.js server bridging Claude ↔ Browser\n- **Browser MCP Client**: WebSocket + REST client in extension\n- **7 MCP Tools**: Claude can discover, query, and control browser\n- **Bi-directional Communication**: Real-time updates and commands\n- **Session Management**: Access feedback sessions from terminal\n\n## Components Added\n\n### MCP Server (mrplug-mcp-server/)\n- src/server.ts - MCP protocol implementation with tools\n- src/browser-plugin-manager.ts - State management\n- src/http-server.ts - WebSocket & REST API server\n- src/stdio-server.ts - Claude Code STDIO transport\n- Full TypeScript support with 147 dependencies\n\n### Browser Extension Integration\n- src/lib/mcp-client.ts - WebSocket client with auto-reconnect\n- src/background/index.ts - MCP client initialization\n- src/types/index.ts - MCP configuration types\n\n### Documentation & Config\n- CLAUDE_INTEGRATION.md - Complete setup guide\n- IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md - Technical details\n- .claude/config.json - Auto-configuration for Claude Code\n- start-mcp-server.sh - Quick start script\n\n## MCP Tools for Claude\n\n1. get_browser_state - Plugin status and active sessions\n2. get_active_session - Full session details\n3. get_element_context - DOM element info (styles, position)\n4. send_browser_command - Control browser (open, select, screenshot)\n5. list_feedback_sessions - List all sessions\n6. query_session_history - Get conversation messages\n7. add_session_message - Add messages to sessions\n\n## Usage\n\n### Start MCP Server\n```bash\ncd mrplug-mcp-server\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\n### Enable in Browser Extension\n- Settings → Enable MCP Integration\n- Server URL: http://localhost:3001\n- WebSocket URL: ws://localhost:3002\n\n### Use with Claude Code\n```\n\"What feedback sessions are active?\"\n\"Show me the button element details\"\n\"Open the browser to that element\"\n```\n\n## Technical Stack\n\n- Model Context Protocol SDK v1.0.4\n- WebSocket (ws) for real-time communication\n- Express for REST API\n- TypeScript with full type safety\n- Auto-reconnection with exponential backoff\n\n## Security Note\n\n⚠️ Current implementation is for LOCAL DEVELOPMENT ONLY\n- No authentication\n- CORS enabled for all origins\n- Designed for localhost use\n\nSee CLAUDE_INTEGRATION.md for production recommendations.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: Add quick start guide for Claude Code integration\n\n* docs: Add comprehensive MCP integration documentation\n\nDocuments the complete MCP + Claude Code integration work including:\n- Full architecture and implementation details\n- All modified files with line references\n- API endpoints and message formats\n- WebSocket streaming implementation\n- Known stability issues and why it was paused\n- Steps to resume in future (estimated 2-3 days)\n\nAlso includes:\n- CURRENT_STATUS.md - Current state and next steps\n- READY_TO_TEST.md - Quick testing guide\n- STREAMING_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md - Guide for Claude Code\n- CLAUDE_CODE_BLOGENGINE_INSTRUCTIONS.md - MCP tool reference\n\nThe MCP integration was functional but deemed too unstable for\ninitial release due to WebSocket complexity, connection management,\nand operational overhead. Preserving all code and documentation\nfor future iteration.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add MCP server and client infrastructure (preserved)\n\nImplements bi-directional communication between browser extension\nand Claude Code via Model Context Protocol server.\n\nMCP Server (mrplug-mcp-server):\n- HTTP REST API on port 3001\n- WebSocket server on port 3002\n- Browser plugin state management\n- Implementation request queue\n- Progress broadcasting system\n\nBrowser Extension Components:\n- MCPClient - WebSocket client for real-time communication\n- MCPDebugPanel - Activity monitor UI component\n- ChatMessage - Enhanced message display with debug info\n- chat-helpers - Message creation utilities\n\nThis infrastructure is preserved but not active in the extension.\nSee docs/MCP_CLAUDE_CODE_INTEGRATION.md for full details.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add GitHub issue integration\n\nEnables creating GitHub issues directly from feedback suggestions.\n\nFeatures:\n- Click GitHub issue suggestions to create issues automatically\n- Full context included in issue body (element, page URL, screenshot)\n- Priority-based labeling (mrplug, priority-high/medium/low)\n- Prompts to configure GitHub token/repo if not set\n- Opens settings page for easy configuration\n\nIssue body includes:\n- User feedback description\n- Element details and context\n- Page URL where feedback originated\n- Screenshot (if available)\n- Created via MrPlug attribution\n\nThis provides a stable, async workflow for implementing fixes\nthrough GitHub''s infrastructure instead of real-time MCP connection.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Add settings page navigation improvements\n\nEnhances settings page UX by returning to the referring tab after saving.\n\nFeatures:\n- Clicking \"Save Settings\" returns to previous browser tab\n- Settings tab closes automatically after save\n- Graceful fallback if referring tab was closed\n- Message handler in background script for open-settings\n\nBackground script (src/background/index.ts):\n- Tracks referring tab ID when opening settings\n- Stores tab ID in local storage\n- Opens existing settings tab if already open\n\nOptions page (src/options/index.tsx):\n- Reads referring tab ID on save\n- Switches back to referring tab\n- Closes settings tab after short delay\n- Cleans up stored tab ID\n\nImproves workflow by reducing tab switching friction when\nconfiguring GitHub tokens or other settings.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Replace MCP integration with GitHub workflow in FeedbackModal\n\nRemoves unstable MCP integration and finalizes GitHub-based workflow.\n\nRemoved:\n- handleClaudeCodeAction() - MCP implementation requests\n- MCP connection status checking\n- MCP activity tracking and debug panel\n- MCP progress event listeners\n- WebSocket message handling\n\nAdded:\n- handleGitHubIssue() - GitHub issue creation from suggestions\n- GitHub configuration prompts\n- Progress messages for issue creation\n- Error handling for GitHub API\n\nChanges:\n- Action handler only supports ''github-issue'' and ''manual'' types\n- Removed ''claude-code'' action type\n- Simplified config loading (no MCP status check)\n- Cleaned up imports (no MCPDebugPanel, ProgressMessages)\n\nThis completes the transition from real-time MCP communication to\nasync GitHub-based workflow, which is more stable and doesn''t\nrequire running a separate MCP server.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* refactor: Delete all MCP implementation code\n\nRemoves all MCP (Model Context Protocol) integration code that was\ndeemed too unstable for initial release.\n\nDeleted:\n- mrplug-mcp-server/ - Complete MCP server directory\n- src/lib/mcp-client.ts - WebSocket client\n- src/components/MCPDebugPanel.tsx - Debug UI\n- src/components/ChatMessage.tsx - MCP-focused message component\n- src/lib/chat-helpers.ts - MCP helper utilities\n- docs/MCP_CLAUDE_CODE_INTEGRATION.md - MCP documentation\n- READY_TO_TEST.md, STREAMING_IMPLEMENTATION_GUIDE.md\n- CLAUDE_CODE_BLOGENGINE_INSTRUCTIONS.md, CURRENT_STATUS.md\n\nChanges to FeedbackModal.tsx:\n- Removed ChatMessage component usage\n- Removed createProgressMessage helper\n- Added simple inline message renderer\n- Added createStatusMessage helper for status updates\n- Simplified message display (no MCP debug info)\n\nRationale:\nMCP integration was functional but unstable due to WebSocket\ncomplexity, connection management issues, and operational overhead.\nFocusing on GitHub-based workflow as a more stable alternative.\n\nA GitHub issue will be created to document what was attempted,\nwhat didn''t work, and potential future improvements.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: gitignore core-managed symlinks (domain-knowledge/, .claude/commands/)\n\nInstalled by core/scripts/install-agents.sh — not owned by this repo.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: Frame OS integration — visual identity, Cmd+Shift+F, AI to background\n\n- Frame tokens: copy shell tokens.css → src/styles/frame-tokens.css (--ojf-* single source)\n- carbon-lite.css now imports frame-tokens instead of hand-rolled vars\n- #mrplug-root always uses cds--g100 — Frame dark, host-page-agnostic\n- Cursor-mode indicator redesigned as fixed top bar (Frame surface, ojf-accent border, slide-in)\n- Command+Shift+F (mac) replaces MacCtrl+Shift+F; Escape added as exit key\n- FeedbackModal heading shows element selector instead of static string\n- Manifest: *.jim.software added to host_permissions + content_scripts\n- AI calls moved from content script to background worker (browser.runtime.sendMessage)\n- Content bundle: 906KB → 254KB (72% reduction — no AI SDK in content)\n- Added CLAUDE.md with invariants and phase roadmap\n- Deleted 14 pre-core-era markdown files from root\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(background): route AI through frame-agent in dev mode\n\nIn dev builds (env.json present), frameAgentUrl is auto-configured to\nhttp://localhost:4001. The ai-request handler tries POST /api/inspect\non frame-agent first; falls back to direct AIAgent if frame-agent is\nunreachable or returns an error — ensuring production users with their\nown API key are unaffected.\n\n- types/index.ts: add frameAgentUrl?: string to ExtensionConfig\n- background/index.ts: frame-agent fetch with graceful fallback;\n  auto-sets frameAgentUrl in both startup and install auto-configure paths\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: wake MV3 service worker on activate to prevent screenshot timeout\n\nThe service worker sleeps after ~30s of inactivity. When the user\nclicks an element, captureVisibleTab() never fires if the SW is cold,\ncausing the 3s timeout to win every time.\n\nFix:\n- activate() sends a fire-and-forget ping to wake the SW while the\n  user is still in cursor mode (before they click anything)\n- background handles ''ping'' → { pong: true } to keep the SW awake\n- timeout raised 3s → 8s to cover SW cold-start (3–5s in practice)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: pre-capture screenshot at command time + fix double-toggle\n\nTwo root causes for missing screenshot thumbnails:\n\n1. captureVisibleTab() requires an activeTab grant, which only exists\n   when the Chrome extension command fires. The content script''s own\n   keydown handler doesn''t grant it. Fix: capture the screenshot\n   immediately in commands.onCommand while activeTab is guaranteed,\n   cache it in pendingScreenshot, and return it on the next\n   ''capture-screenshot'' request. Live capture is kept as fallback.\n\n2. Both the content script keydown handler AND Chrome''s command path\n   call toggleActive(), causing immediate deactivation. Fix: record\n   keydownActivatedAt timestamp; ignore ''toggle-feedback'' messages\n   that arrive within 300ms of a keydown-triggered activation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: expand host_permissions to <all_urls>, update popup for jim.software\n\n- Replace four specific host_permissions with <all_urls> so\n  captureVisibleTab() works from the live-capture fallback path even\n  when the extension was activated via content script keydown (no\n  activeTab grant). Specific host patterns are still enforced by the\n  content_scripts.matches list.\n\n- Popup URL validation: accept *.jim.software in addition to localhost\n  and 127.0.0.1 (matches the content_scripts.matches list)\n\n- Keyboard shortcut help text: Cmd+Shift+F replaces fn-F1, Esc added,\n  copy updated to match actual behaviour\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJpp7vbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA9poQAAt3ix1/ItcYWnMXYVL0xut/\n2p4CCez2sFNa7JjtMs5R/6tjA0raTdv0qQpfMTFoxR5lTh2eB5lDXGamzhI6M+l/\nVm4V5XBx1ZwFJ4Yq/xPkFNyq8zzQGVyjXNGsvM2IkPAXUJv17jv3DoYBoJX75mDI\nRj9Ty1+EQWVKAXie221a7ldq9Z/UJroVIs5IQUGo4Swx10z+Z97MeIO5/+jFknPY\nMCv+wEIdxuUT3GAM84Uxo+KO/s3p6et5Q/+uif92JFODuC/zqe/t6yea+swWRLDJ\nJHehsKg3iVFKqOAlYe6TldLz9oBjQBtrPOm/HGj5PBjYPzIjeo6P5DNR0SC2PuDl\nwhnQM3hM++rZNp7FI7K50eUqrPg3gDJs/E2KAyEynCquoTj/p+SrlIlI6asS0scL\nXHhFawh6nhOeu/EWac8AcI72Fjjca9v5dUGnoNFUQDztS4q1YPeRYNhPZKWMjWNH\n5Frzrm5YPOopMXcWAZ4MqFFnKRS6I/RaSHcty8h+SSfzOL68tCPKVi51QZSdzBde\n98JZWNp9INMg+XSUGaqWI7pgQkCcx7A7YL4yahrKBB/KXhT0V8lrdlIAgn7Sv/lI\n+Kieob3sd1MOiAktYfV2HTzksDrCCSD2xq+LM9hCnKTHKWtJhWBNynNqOdqh4+d8\nUXrLdX6fIzEtYLj7vhOz\n=M2IW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-03-04T04:58:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e","node_id":"C_kwDOQkfx6toAKDc4MTRlMzE0ODkzYWZjNTllNTBmNGQ5NmFlNTg3YTNlMjRjN2QxNGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe","sha":"c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe"}],"sha":"7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/7814e314893afc59e50f4d96ae587a3e24c7d14e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-11T00:14:04Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-11T18:48:08Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"fix: address all must-fix and should-fix issues from PR review\n\nAddresses code review feedback from PR #21 comment #3639334608\n\nMust Fix Issues:\n1. React key stability - Added unique UUID to ConversationMessage interface\n   - Updated all message creation to include Storage.generateUUID()\n   - Changed keys from compound strings to stable msg.id\n   - Fixed FeedbackModal.tsx:653, content/index.tsx:626,666\n\n2. useEffect dependency - Removed loadSessions from dependency array\n   - loadSessions has empty deps, making it stable\n   - Prevents unnecessary effect re-runs (FeedbackModal.tsx:126)\n\n3. XSS sanitization - Sanitize element text content in titles\n   - Remove <> characters and normalize whitespace\n   - Prevents script injection via malicious element content\n   - Updated element-hash.ts:101-104\n\n4. Error handling - Added try-catch for critical session operations\n   - Session creation/resume with user-visible error alerts\n   - Message saving with graceful degradation\n   - Updated content/index.tsx:352-377, 636-646, 681-694\n\nShould Fix Issues:\n5. Optimize sorting - Made getChatSessions sorting optional\n   - getSessionById and findSessionByElementHash skip sorting\n   - Avoids O(n log n) sort for single lookups\n   - Updated storage.ts:72-96\n\n6. Screenshot race condition - Reserve timestamp before waiting\n   - Prevents parallel calls from corrupting rate limit state\n   - Updated content/index.tsx:497-506\n\n7. DOM existence checks - Verify elements in restorePageModal\n   - Prevents errors if page removes modal elements\n   - Updated content/index.tsx:460-464, 475-481\n\n8. Remove non-null assertions - Use local variables instead\n   - Captured sessionId to avoid this.currentSessionId!\n   - Updated content/index.tsx:626-629\n\nAdditional Changes:\n- Made Storage.generateUUID() public for use in message creation\n- Added ChatSession type import to content/index.tsx\n- Fixed test files to include id field in ConversationMessage mocks\n  - storage.test.ts: lines 82, 89, 109, 125\n  - ai-agent.test.ts: lines 99-100\n\nRelated: PR #21, Issue #20","tree":{"sha":"3ff0133f9f8e0b7c851c8e326c95b19007d277b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/trees/3ff0133f9f8e0b7c851c8e326c95b19007d277b5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/commits/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe","node_id":"C_kwDOQkfx6toAKGMxZjgyN2RiMzZjN2NhZDY2ODlmNzY0MmZlNjhkNDJhYjZkNzNjYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8","sha":"1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8"}],"sha":"c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/c1f827db36c7cad6689f7642fe68d42ab6d73cbe"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-10T23:10:58Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-11T18:48:08Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat: integrate session management into feedback modal and content script\n\nIntegrates multithread chat sessions into the user-facing components with\ncomprehensive bug fixes for production readiness.\n\nFeedbackModal Changes:\n- Added SessionList sidebar (250px width, resizable layout)\n- Expanded modal height to 700px to prevent overflow\n- Session switching with immediate UI updates using React.useCallback\n- Auto-focus textarea when modal opens (handles Carbon Design wrapper)\n- Fixed React key props using stable identifiers (timestamp + role + index)\n  to prevent conversation history mismapping across sessions\n- Prevented content script event listeners from interfering with modal input\n- Added comprehensive logging for debugging session switches\n\nContent Script Integration:\n- Element selection creates or resumes session based on hash\n- Session-scoped conversation history replaces global history\n- Screenshot capture with client-side rate limiting (600ms between captures)\n- Subtle page modal dismissal after screenshot capture (300ms opacity fade)\n- Modal state restoration when closing MrPlug modal\n- \"New Session\" button exits to feedback mode for element selection\n\nCritical Bug Fixes:\n- Fixed useEffect dependency causing context re-capture on every message\n- Fixed conversation history mismapping by using stable React keys\n- Fixed keyboard focus interference from page modals (dismissal + restoration)\n- Fixed screenshot rate limit quota errors with graceful degradation\n\nRelated Issues:\n- Closes #20 (partial): Implements workaround for modal focus interference","tree":{"sha":"b69b90e59bfa66087b406459531ad70fc84a82b4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/trees/b69b90e59bfa66087b406459531ad70fc84a82b4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/commits/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8","node_id":"C_kwDOQkfx6toAKDFiNTFjNjEwYjk4ODExOTZiNDI1OWExODk2NjA5ZDMxNWJmNzU1Zjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot/MrPlug/commit/aa7c83c8d2620e7cba2db84e7b18a0286647fb7d","sha":"aa7c83c8d2620e7cba2db84e7b18a0286647fb7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/aa7c83c8d2620e7cba2db84e7b18a0286647fb7d"}],"sha":"1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/1b51c610b9881196b4259a1896609d315bf755f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/commits/aa7c83c8d2620e7cba2db84e7b18a0286647fb7d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-12-10T23:10:37Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-12-11T18:48:08Z","email":"151410806+ojfbot@users.noreply.github.com","name":"ojfbot"},"message":"feat: implement multithread chat sessions with element-based tracking\n\nImplements core infrastructure for maintaining separate conversation sessions\nfor different DOM elements. Each element gets a unique hash-based identifier\nallowing users to resume conversations when re-selecting previously discussed\nelements.\n\nNew Components:\n- ElementHash: FNV-1a hashing for stable element identification\n- SessionSummary: AI-generated summaries with fallback to first message\n- SessionList: UI sidebar component for session navigation\n\nStorage Layer:\n- ChatSession and SessionListItem type definitions\n- CRUD operations for session management (max 20 sessions, 50 messages each)\n- Element hash index for O(1) session lookup\n- Migration from legacy single conversation format\n- Screenshot rate limit error handling to prevent API quota violations\n\nFeatures:\n- Session titles based on element type + content (e.g. \"button: Submit Form\")\n- Last message timestamp tracking for sorting\n- Active session indicator\n- Automatic session cleanup (FIFO when limit reached)","tree":{"sha":"d790bdb30095af7e540fd8981876436cc595ec0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/trees/d790bdb30095af7e540fd8981876436cc595ec0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ojfbot/MrPlug/git/commits/aa7c83c8d2620e7cba2db84e7b18a0286647fb7d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/151410806?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ojfbot/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ojfbot","id":151410806,"login":"ojfbot","node_id":"U_kgDOCQZYdg","organizatio