s_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/RobinKnipe","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/commits/46d99f3c10b83d143e39404ba58bd2a1b3e46be5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T09:04:04Z","email":"robin.knipe@gmail.com","name":"Robin"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T09:04:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: dev security hardening (#83)\n\n* chore: harden repo against NPM supply-chain attack\n* chore: tighten allowed engines, update deps\n* test: fix vi.mock warnings\n* chore: restore save actions, add cspell conf\n* ci: explicitly add ignored npm scripts to actions\n* docs: explain disabling NPM lifecycle scripts\n\n* fix: replace setState-in-effect with pendingValue pattern\nRemoves the useEffect that synchronously called setInputValue(value), which caused cascading renders and violated react-hooks/set-state-in-effect.\n\nReplaces it with a pendingValue state that is null at rest, letting the input derive its display value from `pendingValue ?? value`. This means external changes to the value prop are reflected immediately without any synchronisation logic, and in-progress user input is discarded cleanly on commit.\n\n* chore: opt out of React Compiler memoisation for useReactTable\n\neslint-plugin-react-hooks 7.1.x introduced the react-hooks/incompatible-library rule, which flags useReactTable() as incompatible with automatic memoisation. The compiler already skips the component silently; this makes that decision explicit.\n\nAdded \"use no memo\" to the Table component body and a targeted eslint-disable comment on the useReactTable call to document why optimisation is skipped rather than allowing it to fallback silently.\n\n* chore: extract complexity to shell scripts, following npm script disable.\n* chore: temp install tmp@0.2.6 to fix a critical npm vulnerability\n\nThis is a transitive dependency used by axe.  We had to install this with min-release-age=0 as the vulnerability fix is less than 7 days old.\n\nTo ensure integrity, we have verified that the dist.integrity value on npm matches the tarball hash and that the corresponding commit to fix the vulnerability does actually exist on github.\n\nWe can delete this dependency from 3/5/2026 onwards\n\n* chore: added accessibility-test chrome options to avoid browser crash\n* chore: tweak publish-hotfix to match check pull request\n* chore: added post-install script to keep all install related steps in one place\n* chore: fix hanging playwright install on CI\n* chore: lint fix\n* chore: updated README\n* chore: add husky setup to post-install.sh\n* chore: playwright browser install should be headless (only-shell) on CI, but headed for local `npm test:browser` runs\n* chore: add confirmation step to post install script (local runs)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Paul Gordon <scgpltd@gmail.com>","tree":{"sha":"ebf752b983d26d986a69ac0b3a4085e97eebb541","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/git/trees/ebf752b983d26d986a69ac0b3a4085e97eebb541"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/git/commits/46d99f3c10b83d143e39404ba58bd2a1b3e46be5","verification":{"payload":"tree ebf752b983d26d986a69ac0b3a4085e97eebb541\nparent 543cef17516b3537c1b10959cbf817d4f3d10e06\nauthor Robin <robin.knipe@gmail.com> 1780045444 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1780045444 +0100\n\nchore: dev security hardening (#83)\n\n* chore: harden repo against NPM supply-chain attack\n* chore: tighten allowed engines, update deps\n* test: fix vi.mock warnings\n* chore: restore save actions, add cspell conf\n* ci: explicitly add ignored npm scripts to actions\n* docs: explain disabling NPM lifecycle scripts\n\n* fix: replace setState-in-effect with pendingValue pattern\nRemoves the useEffect that synchronously called setInputValue(value), which caused cascading renders and violated react-hooks/set-state-in-effect.\n\nReplaces it with a pendingValue state that is null at rest, letting the input derive its display value from `pendingValue ?? value`. This means external changes to the value prop are reflected immediately without any synchronisation logic, and in-progress user input is discarded cleanly on commit.\n\n* chore: opt out of React Compiler memoisation for useReactTable\n\neslint-plugin-react-hooks 7.1.x introduced the react-hooks/incompatible-library rule, which flags useReactTable() as incompatible with automatic memoisation. The compiler already skips the component silently; this makes that decision explicit.\n\nAdded \"use no memo\" to the Table component body and a targeted eslint-disable comment on the useReactTable call to document why optimisation is skipped rather than allowing it to fallback silently.\n\n* chore: extract complexity to shell scripts, following npm script disable.\n* chore: temp install tmp@0.2.6 to fix a critical npm vulnerability\n\nThis is a transitive dependency used by axe.  We had to install this with min-release-age=0 as the vulnerability fix is less than 7 days old.\n\nTo ensure integrity, we have verified that the dist.integrity value on npm matches the tarball hash and that the corresponding commit to fix the vulnerability does actually exist on github.\n\nWe can delete this dependency from 3/5/2026 onwards\n\n* chore: added accessibility-test chrome options to avoid browser crash\n* chore: tweak publish-hotfix to match check pull request\n* chore: added post-install script to keep all install related steps in one place\n* chore: fix hanging playwright install on CI\n* chore: lint fix\n* chore: upd