om/users/pgbsl/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pgbsl","id":10134603,"login":"pgbsl","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM0NjAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pgbsl","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/commits/1ea81dfa3fdad4744e7c14c5c3501399fce744d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-13T14:54:17Z","email":"scgpltd@gmail.com","name":"Paul Gordon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-13T14:54:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Feat/route error handling (#51)\n\nAll DAL routes share a similar error handling pattern\n\nErrors, such as 4XX/5XX are thrown from dalRequest(..)\nPartial GraphQL responses are returned from dalRequest(..) with a 200 status code an an errors array\nThe API route handers call dalRequest(..) and map the response received from DAL onto the payload needed for the front end functions.\n\nThis commit adds a new dalApiResponse function that either returns a 200 response with the mapped payload, or if a partial response was received in then the mapped payload is returned, but the partial errors are logged and the HTTP response code supplied to the front end is 206 (Partial Content) to indicate that there may be some data missing.\n\nThe Error thrown from dalRequest is also caught in each route to ensure that an appropriate error response code is sent to the front end.","tree":{"sha":"9f3425e2cda366cc054975ab2738e9da466f59d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/git/trees/9f3425e2cda366cc054975ab2738e9da466f59d3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/DEFRA/fcp-cv-frontend/git/commits/1ea81dfa3fdad4744e7c14c5c3501399fce744d0","verification":{"payload":"tree 9f3425e2cda366cc054975ab2738e9da466f59d3\nparent a0e01ded3b9bb8909d96f8e702aac50d5667a9de\nauthor Paul Gordon <scgpltd@gmail.com> 1776092057 +0100\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1776092057 +0100\n\nFeat/route error handling (#51)\n\nAll DAL routes share a similar error handling pattern\n\nErrors, such as 4XX/5XX are thrown from dalRequest(..)\nPartial GraphQL responses are returned from dalRequest(..) with a 200 status code an an errors array\nThe API route handers call dalRequest(..) and map the response received from DAL onto the payload needed for the front end functions.\n\nThis commit adds a new dalApiResponse function that either returns a 200 response with the mapped payload, or if a partial response was received in then the mapped payload is returned, but the partial errors are logged and the HTTP response code supplied to the front end is 206 (Partial Content) to indicate that there may be some data missing.\n\nThe Error thrown from dalRequest is also caught in each route to ensure that an appropriate error response code is sent to the front end.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp3QOZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAA00QADhaL2UnH9xmPd4FzKcA247o\nELcW2m8PZcFnk0OgTMs7VkPlTMhtijIUW/D4GzMnJAueKGzVs4ONufPUcWbK01MF\n9wUF3WqjKuDtuh4sG3iQtVXcYhK8OwfaJGmjjkWyp9nz8ELBCcjRl++QUCTrsp3Y\nEGsd6UcPWgwJt95tM05QPkMH5+mSSi5hgtYj2q7Bftgmip6BLeDhanuS8TcnSX6a\n4i5jsBw08WgrOhmgZohp16BhM3rH24xSaUqaR69HItDPlxKoWgbo0WXhLvMHYyc8\nhBwT191pCNOMbpcipe1oQEBkoMaToECV63WYnf0tvTBpp5mfN1pbgjdyw6phG/6Z\nHexv3PzDT/0zg7euElKPhCEgxsvJEq6dNukdq/qx7rwtFejSOCZ+gBLOXFdXjDgQ\nCXEZqeh/kVU+x65dm73GvJ+kN1Lt8vIAncdqCIXblFKmN+6emjRaO+NrQfNUdmQL\nmX